speechtext:
Madam Speaker, I rise to exercise my right under Standing Order 43 and to add a footnote to the contemptible and quite irrational remarks of the Prime Minister (Mr. Trudeau) on fascism, which he chose to make outside this House. I therefore move, seconded by the hon. member for Pembina (Mr. Elzinga):
That Canadians be alerted to the fact that the Prime Minister sees
Fascism here;
Fascism there;
Fascism everywhere
But it's in his own chair!
